  data: {
    LLM: "Keep your best cards (Aces, potential pair partners) hidden as long as possible. Reveal cards that make you look weak to induce bluffs, or reveal scary cards to push people out.\n\nIn Dakota, 'buying the option' is essential if you have a powerful wild card (like an Ace as your low-hole) and don't want to risk a Deuce or Three 'replacing' it as the wild rank.\n\nInformation suppression: if you roll a Jack and have another Jack hidden, you are 'representing' a pair but keeping the strength concealed. If you roll two disparate cards, you look like you are chasing a flush/straight.",
    Player: "Keep your best cards (Aces, potential pair partners) hidden as long as possible. Reveal cards that make you look weak to induce bluffs, or reveal scary cards to push people out.\n\nIn Dakota, 'buying the option' is essential if you have a powerful wild card (like an Ace as your low-hole) and don't want to risk a Deuce or Three 'replacing' it as the wild rank.\n\nInformation suppression: if you roll a Jack and have another Jack hidden, you are 'representing' a pair but keeping the strength concealed. If you roll two disparate cards, you look like you are chasing a flush/straight.",
